# AGENTS.md — Lumen Stream Lab (template)

Copy to `AGENTS.md` in your repo root for local Cursor/agent use.  
**Do not commit `AGENTS.md`** — it may contain machine-specific paths. This template is safe to commit.

## Project overview

**Lumen Stream Lab** is an open-source orchestration layer that routes inference across Ollama models to beat the “always use one 3B-class model” baseline on decode throughput.

Read `docs/SCALING.md` and `CONTRIBUTING.md` before hardcoding paths or tok/s.

| Tool | Role |
|------|------|
| **Ollama** | Primary inference backend |
| **Soup** | Training (LoRA + stream_layers) |
| **Lumen router** | Hybrid tiers (1B / LFM / domain 3B / 7B) |

**Do not confuse** “Lumen Stream Lab” (this project) with Laravel Lumen (PHP).

## Primary metric

+40% mean decode tok/s vs always `llama3.2:3b` on **your** hardware. Reference numbers: `hardware/reference-lab.json`, `docs/REFERENCE-RESULTS.md`.

```bash
python3 scripts/compare.py --baseline 48.38 --optimized 70.0 --min-gain 0.40
```

## Routing (keep in sync)

When changing routing rules, update **both**:

1. `deploy/win-router-lib.ps1`
2. `lumen_router.py`

```bash
python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v
python3 lumen.py route --prompt "What is Lumen Stream Lab?"
```

